input_prompt: Explain what on-device AI means in simple terms.
INFO: Loaded OpenCL library with dlopen.


On-device AI means using AI models that run directly on your device, like a phone or computer, instead of relying on a server or cloud. This means you can train the model with the data you already have on your device, which saves space and power. For example, if you use a fitness app, it learns from your own data (like your heart rate and steps) to make recommendations without needing to access the internet. This makes the AI more efficient and personalized for you.

